  "visualBrief": "Amsterdam Centraal pairs the red-brick Cuypers frontage, wind dial, clock, gables and mansards with three arched rail sheds. Glazed end screens leave the tracks open below. The modern IJ-side bus canopy spans its raised deck, with the red AMSTERDAM lettering formed in the glass.",
  "heightPolicy": "The six-meter sea-level datum follows standard viewer terrain. The masonry bases reach the sampled station island and six platform strips follow local grades with boarding edges clear of mapped rail lines.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X follows the platforms east-southeast. Positive Z faces the Stationsplein and Damrak city side. Negative Z faces the IJ and the bus canopy.",
  "limitations": [
    "The PMTiles footprints set the position of the historic frontage and four long roofs. The six-meter datum follows standard viewer terrain. Facade ornaments and most elevations are exterior photo estimates.",
    "The exterior includes the visible platform canopies, glazed end screens, rail platforms and the raised IJ bus deck. Platform fittings and roof lettering are simplified at viewer scale. Active rail, streets, ferry water and surrounding buildings stay in the underlying map."
  ],
